description:
What: Define RnewsConfig — a stripped-down config for stoa-rnews that does NOT require [listen], [gc], or [pinning].
File: new crates/transit/src/rnews_config.rs; add pub mod rnews_config to crates/transit/src/lib.rs.
Algorithm:
1. Create crates/transit/src/rnews_config.rs
2. Re-use existing types from crates/transit/src/config.rs: DatabaseConfig, BackendConfig, IpfsConfig, LogConfig, GroupsConfig, OperatorConfig.
3. Define:
   #[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]
   pub struct RnewsConfig {
     pub database: DatabaseConfig,        // reuse existing — already has defaults
     pub backend: Option<BackendConfig>,  // optional: if absent + no ipfs.url, fail validation
     pub ipfs: Option<IpfsConfig>,        // legacy fallback
     pub groups: Option<GroupsConfig>,    // None = accept all groups
     pub operator: OperatorConfig,        // needs signing_key_path and hostname
     pub log: LogConfig,                  // reuse existing — has defaults
   }
   impl RnewsConfig {
     pub fn from_file(path: &Path) -> Result<Self, ConfigError> { ... }
     pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), ConfigError> {
       // Must have either backend or ipfs.url — else fail
       // Must NOT require listen, gc, or pinning
     }
   }
4. Add pub mod rnews_config to lib.rs.
Defensive rules: Config parse errors must return ConfigError (not panic). Use serde(default) for optional fields with sensible defaults.
Tests:
- test_rnews_config_minimal_valid: parse TOML with only database+backend+operator fields; assert Ok
- test_rnews_config_no_listen_required: no [listen] section; assert Ok
- test_rnews_config_fails_without_storage: no backend and no ipfs.url; assert Err
